 combinations previously effectively published outside the IJSB. Int J Syst Bacteriol 1991; 41:456-457.\n\nNomenclatural status: not validly published, basonym of name in Approved Lists\n\nTaxonomic status: synonym (and no standing)\n\nCorrect name: Streptomyces lilacinus (Nakazawa et al. 1956) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991\n\nRisk group: 1\n\n  * Synonyms:\n    * Name  | Kind\n--- | ---\nStreptoverticillium kashmirense corrig. (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Locci et al. 1969 (Approved Lists 1980)  | heterotypic synonym, validly published under the ICNP\n\"Verticillomyces lilacinus\" (Nakazawa et al. 1956) Shinobu 1965  | homotypic synonym, not validly published\nStreptoverticillium kashmirensis (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Locci et al. 1969 (Approved Lists 1980)  | heterotypic synonym, inaccurate spelling\nStreptomyces kashimirensis (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991  | heterotypic synonym, inaccurate spelling\nStreptomyces kashmirensis corrig. (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991  | heterotypic synonym, validly published under the ICNP\n\"Streptomyces kashmirensis\" Gupta and Chopra 1963  | heterotypic synonym, not validly published, basonym of name in Approved Lists\nStreptoverticillium lilacinum (Nakazawa et al. 1956) Locci et al. 1969 (Approved Lists 1980)  | homotypic synonym, validly published under the ICNP\nStreptomyces lilacinus (Nakazawa et al. 1956) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991  | homotypic synonym, validly published under the ICNP\n\n  * Notes:\n    * ⏰ According to Hatano et al. (2003), this species is an earlier heterotypic synonym of Streptoverticillium kashmirensis (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Locci et al. 1969 (Approved Lists 1980). Publication: Hatano K, Nishii T, Kasai H. Taxonomic re-evaluation of whorl-forming Streptomyces (formerly Streptoverticillium) species by using phenotypes, DNA-DNA hybridization and sequences of gyrB, and proposal of Streptomyces luteireticuli (ex Katoh and Arai 1957) corrig., sp. nov., nom. rev. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol 2003; 53:1519-1529. 🇯🇵 (Japan)\n    * ⏰ According to Hatano et al. (2003), this species is an earlier heterotypic synonym of \"Streptomyces kashmirensis\" Gupta and Chopra 1963. Publication: Hatano K, Nishii T, Kasai H. Taxonomic re-evaluation of whorl-forming Streptomyces (formerly Streptoverticillium) species by using phenotypes, DNA-DNA hybridization and sequences of gyrB, and proposal of Streptomyces luteireticuli (ex Katoh and Arai 1957) corrig., sp. nov., nom. rev. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol 2003; 53:1519-1529. 🇯🇵 (Japan)\n    * ⏰ According to Hatano et al. (2003), this species is an earlier heterotypic synonym of Streptoverticillium kashmirense corrig. (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Locci et al. 1969 (Approved Lists 1980). Publication: Hatano K, Nishii T, Kasai H. Taxonomic re-evaluation of whorl-forming Streptomyces (formerly Streptoverticillium) species by using phenotypes, DNA-DNA hybridization and sequences of gyrB, and proposal of Streptomyces luteireticuli (ex Katoh and Arai 1957) corrig., sp. nov., nom. rev. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol 2003; 53:1519-1529. 🇯🇵 (Japan)\n    * ⏰ According to Hatano et al. (2003), this species is an earlier heterotypic synonym of Streptomyces kashimirensis (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991. Publication: Hatano K, Nishii T, Kasai H. Taxonomic re-evaluation of whorl-forming Streptomyces (formerly Streptoverticillium) species by using phenotypes, DNA-DNA hybridization and sequences of gyrB, and proposal of Streptomyces luteireticuli (ex Katoh and Arai 1957) corrig., sp. nov., nom. rev. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol 2003; 53:1519-1529. 🇯🇵 (Japan)\n    * ⏰ According to Hatano et al. (2003), this species is an earlier heterotypic synonym of Streptomyces kashmirensis corrig. (Gupta and Chopra 1963) Witt and Stackebrandt 1991. Publication: Hatano K, Nishii T, Kasai H. Taxonomic re-evaluation of whorl-forming Streptomyces (formerly Streptoverticillium) species by using phenotypes, DNA-DNA hybridization and sequences of gyrB, and proposal of Streptomyces luteireticuli (ex Katoh and Arai 1957) corrig., sp. nov., nom. rev. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol 2003; 53:1519-1529. 🇯🇵 (Japan)\n    * 😷 The risk group for Canada has been imported on 2024-02-27. The full classification is: risk group = 1, note = \"Security sensitive biological agent: No - Terrestrial animal pathogen under Canadian Food Inspection Agency authority: No\". — The risk group for Swiss Confederation has been imported on 2024-02-01. The full classification is: risk group = 1. — The risk group for Germany has been imported on 2026-08-13. The full classification is: risk group = 1. — If in doubt, use the risk group given in the regulations for your country and, if these are not available, use the risk group given in the catalogue of the culture collection from which you have obtained or intend to obtain the strain.\n\nParent taxon: Streptomyces Waksman and Henrici 1943 (Approved Lists 1980)\n\nAssigned by: Nakazawa K, Tanabe K, Shibata M, Miyake A, Takewaka T. Studies on streptomycetes. Cladomycin, a new antibiotic produced by Streptomyces lilacinus nov. sp. Journal of Antibiotics (Tokyo) Series B 1956; 9:81.\n\nLinking: To permanently link to this page, use https://doi.org/10.83108/rn.4059[Button: Copy to clipboard]Link copied to clipboard\n\nRecord number: 4059--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDetails - Leibniz Institute DSMZ (https://www.dsmz.de/collection/catalogue/details/culture/DSM-40190)\nciteturn16search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Produces restriction endonuclease SgoI (XhoI) (2358), bandamycin A, B, pentaene antibiotic.\n\nHomeCollectionCatalogue\n\nImage: Bacteria\n\n# Streptomyces goshikiensis\n\nDSM 40190\n\nBACTERIA\n\nImage How to read the following data (Example)\n\nName:\n\nStreptomyces goshikiensis Niida 1966\n\nDSM No.:\n\n40190, Type strain dsm-40190 dsm40190 dsm 40190 Streptomyces goshikiensis\n\nStrain designation:\n\nISP 5190\n\nOther collection no.\nor WDCM no.:\n\nATCC 23914,CBS 835.68,IFO 12868,RIA 1144,NBRC 12868\n\nIsolated from:\n\nsoil\n\nCountry:\n\nJapan\n\nDate of sampling:\n\nbefore 22.08.1990\n\nNagoya Protocol Restrictions:\n\nThere are NO known Nagoya Protocol restrictions for this strain.\n\nHistory:\n\n<- E.B. Shirling, ISP <- M. Oda, Meiji Seiko Co\n\nCultivation conditions:\n\nMedium 65 , 28°C\nComplete DSMZ Media List\n\nSummary and\nadditional information:\n\n<- E.B. Shirling, ISP <- M. Oda, Meiji Seiko Co. Soil; Japan. Type strain (1300). Produces restriction endonuclease SgoI (XhoI) (2358), bandamycin A, B, pentaene antibiotic. (Medium 65, 28°C).\n\nWink compendium:\n\nDSM 40190.pdf\n\nLiterature:\n\n1300, 2358\n\nRisk group:\n\n1 (classification according to German TRBA)\n\nSupplied as:\n\nDelivery form  |    | Prices\nFreeze Dried  |    | 120,- €\nActive culture on request  |    | 280,- €\nDNA  |    | 180,- €  |  \nPrice Category for this culture: 1\nFreight and handling charges will be added. See price list.\n\nOther cultures:\n\nAll DSMZ cultures of the species\n\n \n\nPrint data sheet\n\nAdd to Cart Open Pricelist--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGerman Collection of Microorganisms and Cell Cultures GmbH: Welcome to the Leibniz Institute DSMZ | Streptomyces goshikiensis (https://webshop.dsmz.de/en/bacteria/Streptomyces-goshikiensis.html)\nciteturn16search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Produces restriction endonuclease SgoI (XhoI) (2358), bandamycin A, B, pentaene antibiotic.\n\n# Streptomyces goshikiensis\n\nProduct number: DSM 40190\n\nSelection:\n\nSelection Choose variant [Input]\n\nfrom 120,00 €\n\nPlease log in.\n\n  * Add to notepad\n\n   |  \n--- | ---\n | Detailed Price Information Link\nBACTERIA  | Image How to read the following data (Example)\nName:  | Streptomyces goshikiensis Niida 1966\nDSM No.:  | 40190, Type strain dsm-40190 dsm40190 dsm 40190 Streptomyces goshikiensis\nStrain designation:  | ISP 5190\nOther collection no.\nor WDCM no.:  | ATCC 23914,CBS 835.68,IFO 12868,RIA 1144,NBRC 12868\nIsolated from:  | soil\nCountry:  | Japan\nDate of sampling:  | before 22.08.1990\nNagoya Protocol Restrictions:  | There are NO known Nagoya Protocol restrictions for this strain.\nHistory:  | <- E.B. Shirling, ISP <- M. Oda, Meiji Seiko Co\nCultivation conditions:  | Medium 65 , 28°C\nComplete DSMZ Media List\nSummary and\nadditional information:  | <- E.B. Shirling, ISP <- M. Oda, Meiji Seiko Co. Soil; Japan. Type strain (1300). Produces restriction endonuclease SgoI (XhoI) (2358), bandamycin A, B, pentaene antibiotic. (Medium 65, 28°C).\nWink compendium:  | DSM 40190.pdf\nLiterature:  | 1300, 2358\nRisk group:  | 1 (classification according to German TRBA)\nSupplied as:  | \nDelivery form   Prices\nFreeze Dried   120,- €\nActive culture on request   280,- €\nDNA   180,- €  \nPrice Category for this culture: 1\nFreight and handling charges will be added. See price list.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVOL\nXXII\nNO\n9\nTHE\nJOURNAL\nOF\nANTIBIOTIC?\n4O9\nSTUDI (https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibiotics1968/22/9/22_9_409/_pdf)\nciteturn16search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; ANTIBIOTICS ... antimicrobial ... antibiotic. ... danubomycin and process\nVOL.\nXXII\nNO.\n9\nTHE\nJOURNAL\nOF\nANTIBIOTICS\n417\nobviously\ndiffers\nfrom\nthese\nantibiotics\nin\nits\nelememtary\nanalysis,\nultraviolet\nspectrum,\ninfrared\nspectrum,\ncolor\nreactions\nand\nantimicrobial\nspectrum.\nAcknowledgments\nThe authors\nwish\nto express\ntheir\ngratitude\nto\nDr. S. Tatsuoka\nfor\nhis\nencouragement\nand to\nDrs.\nR. Takeda,\nK. Nakazawa, A. Miyake and K. Mizuno for their\nadvice.\nThanks are\nalso\ndue to\ntheir\nco-workers for elementary\nanalyses,\nmeasurement of physicochemical\nproperties\nand conduct of\ntank fermentation.\nThanks are also\ndue to Mrs. T. Mori for\nher assistance.\nReferences\n1) Yamaguchi, T. & Y. Sa